/* ---------- init ---------- */
for (var i = 0; i < panels.length; i++) buildPanel(panels[i]);
runText(mDraw, 12, 4, [
  { t: 'P', sans: 1, fill: C.gray }, { t: 'atm', sub: 1, sans: 1, fill: C.gray },
  { t: '\u00a0=\u00a0760\u00a0torr', sans: 1, fill: C.gray }
], 14, false, 'start');

applyOpacity();
renderPanels();
applyStep(0);

window.__markRendered();
// @FIGURE_CODE_END

Fix all identified failure modes and improve every score. Maintain or improve what already works well.
Return ONLY the updated marker-wrapped payload.

userContent.text:
Build an interactive figure using SVG.js.

CONCEPT: A manometer measures an unknown gas pressure by balancing it against a mercury column, and which of three equations applies (P_gas = hρg, P_atm − hρg, or P_atm + hρg) depends entirely on whether the reference arm is a vacuum or open to the atmosphere and which arm's mercury stands higher.
KEY INSIGHT (what students should walk away understanding): A manometer never measures pressure directly — it measures a pressure DIFFERENCE as a mercury height; whether you add h, subtract h, or use h alone depends only on what is pressing down on the other arm (vacuum or atmosphere) and which column ended up higher.
DEMO STEPS: 6 guided steps — implement the step player in #ui

FULL BLUEPRINT:
